= Price impact — Simple =

Price impact is how much your own trade moves the market price. It is usually larger when the trade is big compared with nearby liquidity. Price impact is not identical to all slippage.

'''Important boundary:''' price impact ≠ slippage.

== Sources ==
* Albert S. Kyle, “Continuous Auctions and Insider Trading” (1985), for market-depth/price-impact foundations.
